  data:  # a84f
    kind: work_item  # a84f
    title: "Per-file analyzer memoization keyed on (git blob sha + complete input key); reuse on unchanged files"  # a84f
    status: todo_soft  # a84f
    priority: 3  # a84f
    parent:  # a84f
    tags:  # a84f
    - perf  # a84f
    - cache  # a84f
    isbefore: []  # a84f
    duplicate_of: []  # a84f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # a84f
    pr_ref:  # a84f
    description: "DEFERRED — gated on MEAS-1 proving full-run latency actually hurts. Do NOT build until the number demands it.\n\nIdea: per-file analyzer output is (mostly) a pure function of the file's own bytes, so memoize it. Git blob SHAs ARE content hashes -> the natural cache key. A 3-file PR then re-parses 3 files; the embarrassingly-parallel parse cost collapses to the diff size.\n\nNon-trivial to prove + implement:\n- SOUNDNESS: per-file extract must be a PURE function of that file's bytes. Any analyzer that peeks cross-file (imported symbol kind, base class elsewhere, re-export) breaks it -> verify purity analyzer-by-analyzer; it silently regresses. Global identity reconciliation (split_within_file_stable_id_collisions / widen_route_stable_ids / synthetic-class-B) is whole-graph and re-runs regardless.\n- COMPLETE KEY: the key is (blob_sha, analyzer_version, GRAMMAR version, config, ...) — miss one input -> silent stale hit (worst failure mode).\n- DETERMINISM precondition: only safe to cache a deterministic function's output -> requires the `--reproducible` mode (WI-sazap).\n- IRREDUCIBLE REMAINDER: the LINKERS (cross-file edge recovery) still run whole-graph — memoization only attacks the parse/extract stage, NOT total work.\n\n\"Proof\" = a differential equivalence property test: incremental_run(repo, arbitrary change-set) == full_run(repo), canonical-compared over the bakeoff corpus (reuses WI-sazap's byte-identity guard). Build THIS first — until it is green, blob-SHA memoization is a silent-corruption generator.\n\nBlocked-by: MEAS-1 (proves need) + WI-sazap (determinism + the differential guard). See also INC-2 (cheaper coarse-grained precursor)."  # a84f
    fields: {}  # a84f
- op: discuss  # 71ac
  at: '2026-08-17T08:37:50Z'  # 71ac
  by: agent  # 71ac
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 71ac
  clock: 2  # 71ac
  nonce: 71ac  # 71ac
  message: "STILL CORRECTLY DEFERRED, and now for a measured reason rather than an absent\none. Partial MEAS-1 landed 2026-08-17 (numbers and caveats on WI-kazas):\n\n  small 33 s | medium 119 s | large 201 s | MONOREPO 489 s\n\nThis item's gate is WI-kazas's third band, \"tens of minutes on a monorepo ->\nfile-level memoization earns its keep\". The monorepo cell came in at 8.2\nminutes. That is the second band, which selects WI-zagij (package scoping), not\nthis. I am not stretching 8.2 minutes into \"tens of minutes\" to unblock the more\ninteresting item — the whole point of the gate was to stop exactly that.\n\nWHAT WOULD ACTUALLY UNGATE THIS, both already filed:\n- WI-rukaz: a ~14.6k-file Java repo running >60 min with the bottleneck\n  unlocated. If that reproduces it IS the \"tens of minutes\" cell and this item\n  ungates immediately. Worth measuring before building anything here.\n- The analysis-vs-linking split of a cold run. This item already names the\n  linkers as the \"irreducible remainder\"; if linking dominates, NEITHER this\n  nor WI-zagij helps much and the target is the linker stage instead. The\n  per-pass timers in AnalysisRun make this cheap.\n\nONE PIECE OF EVIDENCE FOR THIS ITEM'S SOUNDNESS HAZARD, observed incidentally.\nThe cache's `<analyzer_identity>` segment hashes the CONTENT of every installed\nhypergumbo_* .py file, so adding a single comment to edge_types.py moves it\n(09f205d121a3680a -> c0784fc9dcd9a62a, and back on revert). That is the correct\nbehaviour for that segment and it is NOT what makes smart-test slow — smart-test\nuses the pipx $STABLE_HG, whose identity is constant. It is recorded here only\nbecause it demonstrates the \"COMPLETE KEY\" hazard this item warns about is real\nand already being handled at whole-tree granularity: a per-file key has to carry\nevery one of those inputs, and the failure mode is a silent stale hit."  # 71ac
- op: discuss  # 0a9c
