  nonce: ed9e  # ed9e
  message: "OWNER RULING (2026-08-17), verbatim: \"I guess we've mined all the processing\nefficiency that's reasonable to mine at this point in the hypergumbo project.\"\n\nPARKED — wont_do + someday. Not \"won't ever\"; \"not at this point in the project\".\nThis item is intact and its ceiling is measured, so re-opening is a status change,\nnot a re-derivation.\n\nWHAT WAS ACTUALLY MINED, so nobody re-measures it:\n  cold run_survey on this monorepo   517.7s -> 139.1s   (3.7x)\n    #394  fingerprint locator was quadratic in file size   -297.7s (62.6% of wall)\n    #395  --minimal declines side outputs a caller never reads   -59.1s\n    #397  one shared CLI scan instead of four                    -23.3s\n\nWHY THIS ONE IS PARKED RATHER THAN BUILT. Its own ceiling is favourable — the\nanalyzer phase is ~96% per-file (65.7s uncapped vs 2.6s at max_files=1), so a\nper-file cache could reach ~3s and take the run to ~97s. What disqualifies it is\nCOST OF CORRECTNESS, not size of prize: it is blocked-by WI-sazap (unbuilt), needs\na per-analyzer purity audit, and its own filed acceptance bar is a differential\nequivalence test over the bakeoff corpus built FIRST, because until that is green\nblob-SHA memoization is a silent-corruption generator. The owner's condition was\n\"as long as that work seems straightforward\". It is not.\n\nRE-OPEN TRIGGER (unchanged): WI-rukaz reproducing a >60min run, i.e. the \"tens of\nminutes on a monorepo\" band this item's gate always named. This repo is 139.1s.\nIf it re-opens, build the differential test before any caching code."  # ed9e
